<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1 </span>Definition and Assumption</h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As the premise, we give <span id="S4.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ 4.1 Definition and Assumption ‣ 4 MFL Performance Analysis ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></span>-<a href="#Thmassumption4" title="Assumption 4. ‣ 4.1 Definition and Assumption ‣ 4 MFL Performance Analysis ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_bold"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> corresponding to <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(\bm{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\bm{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math> as follows.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmassumption1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmassumption1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 1</span></span><span id="Thmassumption1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmassumption1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmassumption1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmassumption1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The global loss function is <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-smooth, i.e., <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla H(\bm{\theta})-\!\nabla H(\bm{\varphi})\|\!\leq\gamma\|\bm{\theta}-\bm{\varphi}\|,\forall\bm{\theta},\bm{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝛉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.052em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝛗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.108em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝛉</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝛗</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>𝛉</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">ϕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla H(\bm{\theta})-\!\nabla H(\bm{\varphi})\|\!\leq\gamma\|\bm{\theta}-\bm{\varphi}\|,\forall\bm{\theta},\bm{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmassumption2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmassumption2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 2</span></span><span id="Thmassumption2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmassumption2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmassumption2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmassumption2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The global loss function is <math id="Thmassumption2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz continuous, i.e., <math id="Thmassumption2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|H(\bm{\theta})-H(\bm{\varphi})|\leq\rho\|\bm{\theta}-\bm{\varphi}\|,\forall\bm{\theta},\bm{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝛉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝛗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝛉</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝛗</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>𝛉</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">ϕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|H(\bm{\theta})-H(\bm{\varphi})|\leq\rho\|\bm{\theta}-\bm{\varphi}\|,\forall\bm{\theta},\bm{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmassumption3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmassumption3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 3</span></span><span id="Thmassumption3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmassumption3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmassumption3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmassumption3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The norm of the local unimodal subgradient is bounded by <math id="Thmassumption3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla H(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})\|\leq\zeta_{m}^{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝛉</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla H(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})\|\leq\zeta_{m}^{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmassumption4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmassumption4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 4</span></span><span id="Thmassumption4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmassumption4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmassumption4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmassumption4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The norm of the difference between the global unimodal subgradient and the local unimodal subgradient is bounded by <math id="Thmassumption4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla H_{k}(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})-\nabla H(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})\|\leq\delta_{k,m}^{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝛉</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝛉</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla H_{k}(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})-\nabla H(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})\|\leq\delta_{k,m}^{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Inspired by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">31</a>, <a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">33</a>]</cite>, the characteristics of the multimodal model are described in <span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 1</span> and <span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 2</span>, whereas <span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 3</span> and <span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 4</span> outline the training processes of different unimodal models.</span> In addition, we define a virtual auxiliary parameter to server a bridge between the global multimodal models in the adjacent communication rounds.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 1</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The virtual auxiliary parameter <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\psi}_{m}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝛙</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\psi}_{m}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is updated by local multimodal gradients of all clients, i.e., <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{\psi}_{m}^{t}\triangleq\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1}-\eta\sum_{k=1}^{K}\bar{w}_{k,m}\nabla H_{k}(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})=\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1}-\eta\nabla H(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝛙</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>≜</mo><msubsup><mi>𝛉</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝛉</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝛉</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝛉</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\psi}_{m}^{t}\triangleq\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1}-\eta\sum_{k=1}^{K}\bar{w}_{k,m}\nabla H_{k}(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})=\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1}-\eta\nabla H(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1}).</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2 </span>Main Results</h3>

<div id="Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The difference between <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(\bm{\theta}^{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝛉</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\bm{\theta}^{t})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(\bm{\psi}^{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝛙</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\bm{\psi}^{t})</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded by</span></p>
<table id="S4.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(\bm{\theta}^{t})-H(\bm{\psi}^{t})\leq{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\eta\rho\sqrt{A_{1}^{t}+A_{2}^{t}}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝝍</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\bm{\theta}^{t})-H(\bm{\psi}^{t})\leq{\color[rgb]{0,0,0}\eta\rho\sqrt{A_{1}^{t}+A_{2}^{t}}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{1}^{t}\triangleq\sum_{m\notin\mathcal{M}^{t}}(\zeta_{m}^{t-1})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.111em">≜</mo><mrow><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∉</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℳ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msup></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ζ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{1}^{t}\triangleq\sum_{m\notin\mathcal{M}^{t}}(\zeta_{m}^{t-1})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{2}^{t}\triangleq\sum_{m\in\mathcal{M}^{t}}[2(1-\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}_{m}}a_{k}^{t}\bar{w}_{k,m})\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}_{m}}(w^{t}_{k,m}\!\!+\bar{w}_{k,m}\!\!-2a_{k}^{t}\bar{w}_{k,m})(\delta_{k,m}^{t-1})^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.111em">≜</mo><mrow><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℳ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒦</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒦</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{2}^{t}\triangleq\sum_{m\in\mathcal{M}^{t}}[2(1-\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}_{m}}a_{k}^{t}\bar{w}_{k,m})\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}_{m}}(w^{t}_{k,m}\!\!+\bar{w}_{k,m}\!\!-2a_{k}^{t}\bar{w}_{k,m})(\delta_{k,m}^{t-1})^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math> for concise expression.<span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para"><span id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">{IEEEproof}</span>
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Please refer to the detailed proof in Appendix <a href="#A0.SS1" title=".1 Proof of Theorem 1 ‣ 7 Conclusions ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In <span id="S4.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1</span>, all clients participation makes the whole term equal 0, which is consistent with reality. We can also see that <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> modalities act together in the upper bound. <span id="S4.SS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">If <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{m}^{t-1}\gg\delta_{k,m}^{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ζ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≫</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{m}^{t-1}\gg\delta_{k,m}^{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, modality <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> will contribute more significantly to the bound value in <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{1}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{1}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> than <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{2}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{2}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, the scheduling decision will emphasize modality <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> to avoid large bound values. In contrast, if <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta_{m}^{t-1}\ll\delta_{k,m}^{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ζ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≪</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta_{m}^{t-1}\ll\delta_{k,m}^{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, modality <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> will have a greater impact on the bound value in <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{2}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{2}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> than in <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{1}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{1}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. And the scheduling decision will consider suspending training on modality <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> in favor of clients with other modalities. A large <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{k,m}^{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{k,m}^{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math> indicates that <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\theta}^{t-1}_{{\rm g},m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝜽</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">g</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\theta}^{t-1}_{{\rm g},m}</annotation></semantics></math> is necessary and preferred during client scheduling.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 2</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The descend of the loss function in a communication round is bounded by</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle H(\bm{\theta}^{t})-H(\bm{\theta}^{t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle H(\bm{\theta}^{t})-H(\bm{\theta}^{t-1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq-\frac{2\eta-\gamma\eta^{2}}{2}\sum_{m=1}^{M}\|\nabla H(\bm{\theta}^{t-1}_{{\rm g},m})\|^{2}+\eta\rho\sqrt{A_{1}^{t}+A_{2}^{t}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mi>η</mi><mi>ρ</mi><msqrt><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq-\frac{2\eta-\gamma\eta^{2}}{2}\sum_{m=1}^{M}\|\nabla H(\bm{\theta}^{t-1}_{{\rm g},m})\|^{2}+\eta\rho\sqrt{A_{1}^{t}+A_{2}^{t}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para"><span id="S4.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">{IEEEproof}</span>
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Firstly, the difference between a communication round is taken into consideration as</p>
<table id="S4.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(\bm{\theta}^{t})-H(\bm{\theta}^{t-1})=(H(\bm{\theta}^{t})-H(\bm{\psi}^{t}))+(H(\bm{\psi}^{t})-H(\bm{\theta}^{t-1}))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝝍</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝝍</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\bm{\theta}^{t})-H(\bm{\theta}^{t-1})=(H(\bm{\theta}^{t})-H(\bm{\psi}^{t}))+(H(\bm{\psi}^{t})-H(\bm{\theta}^{t-1})).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Now that <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(\bm{\theta}^{t})-H(\bm{\psi}^{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝝍</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\bm{\theta}^{t})-H(\bm{\psi}^{t})</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded in <span id="S4.SS2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 4.2 Main Results ‣ 4 MFL Performance Analysis ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></span>, we can concentrate on <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(\bm{\psi}^{t})-H(\bm{\theta}^{t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝝍</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\bm{\psi}^{t})-H(\bm{\theta}^{t-1})</annotation></semantics></math>. According to the property of <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-smooth in <span id="S4.SS2.p3.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ 4.1 Definition and Assumption ‣ 4 MFL Performance Analysis ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></span>, we have</p>
<table id="S4.E25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(\bm{\psi}^{t})-H(\bm{\theta}^{t-1})\leq\langle H(\bm{\theta}^{t-1}),\bm{\psi}^{t}-\bm{\theta}^{t-1}\rangle+\frac{\gamma}{2}\|\bm{\psi}^{t}-\bm{\theta}^{t-1}\|^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝝍</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝝍</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝝍</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\bm{\psi}^{t})-H(\bm{\theta}^{t-1})\leq\langle H(\bm{\theta}^{t-1}),\bm{\psi}^{t}-\bm{\theta}^{t-1}\rangle+\frac{\gamma}{2}\|\bm{\psi}^{t}-\bm{\theta}^{t-1}\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.4" class="ltx_p">The square norm term can be expanded into a sum over <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> modalities as</p>
<table id="S4.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\gamma}{2}\|\bm{\psi}^{t}-\bm{\theta}^{t-1}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝝍</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\gamma}{2}\|\bm{\psi}^{t}-\bm{\theta}^{t-1}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\gamma\eta^{2}}{2}\|\nabla H(\bm{\theta}^{t-1})\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\gamma\eta^{2}}{2}\|\nabla H(\bm{\theta}^{t-1})\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\gamma\eta^{2}}{2}\sum_{m=1}^{M}\|\nabla H(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})\|^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\gamma\eta^{2}}{2}\sum_{m=1}^{M}\|\nabla H(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.5" class="ltx_p">Similarly, the inner product term can be rewritten by</p>
<table id="S4.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\langle H(\bm{\theta}^{t-1}),\bm{\psi}^{t}-\bm{\theta}^{t-1}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝝍</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\langle H(\bm{\theta}^{t-1}),\bm{\psi}^{t}-\bm{\theta}^{t-1}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex6.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\!=\!\langle\nabla H(\bm{\theta}^{t-1}),-\eta\nabla H(\bm{\theta}^{t-1})\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\!=\!\langle\nabla H(\bm{\theta}^{t-1}),-\eta\nabla H(\bm{\theta}^{t-1})\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E27.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\eta\sum_{m=1}^{M}\Big\|\nabla H(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})\Big\|^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>η</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.600em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.600em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.0835em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\eta\sum_{m=1}^{M}\Big\|\nabla H(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})\Big\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.6" class="ltx_p">Substituting (<a href="#S4.E26" title="In 4.2 Main Results ‣ 4 MFL Performance Analysis ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>) and (<a href="#S4.E27" title="In 4.2 Main Results ‣ 4 MFL Performance Analysis ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a>) into (<a href="#S4.E25" title="In 4.2 Main Results ‣ 4 MFL Performance Analysis ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>), we have</p>
<table id="S4.E28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E28.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="H(\bm{\psi}^{t})-H(\bm{\theta}^{t-1})\leq-\frac{2\eta-\gamma\eta^{2}}{2}\sum_{m=1}^{M}\|\nabla H(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})\|^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝝍</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.0835em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\bm{\psi}^{t})-H(\bm{\theta}^{t-1})\leq-\frac{2\eta-\gamma\eta^{2}}{2}\sum_{m=1}^{M}\|\nabla H(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.7" class="ltx_p">Substituting (<a href="#S4.E28" title="In 4.2 Main Results ‣ 4 MFL Performance Analysis ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>) into (<a href="#S4.E24" title="In 4.2 Main Results ‣ 4 MFL Performance Analysis ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>) and applying <span id="S4.SS2.p3.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 4.2 Main Results ‣ 4 MFL Performance Analysis ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></span>, we can prove <span id="S4.SS2.p3.7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem <a href="#S4.EGx4" title="Theorem 2. ‣ 4.2 Main Results ‣ 4 MFL Performance Analysis ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></span>.

The first term on the right side in <span id="S4.SS2.p3.7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem <a href="#S4.EGx4" title="Theorem 2. ‣ 4.2 Main Results ‣ 4 MFL Performance Analysis ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></span> is negative and unrelated to <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{a}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{a}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, the descend of the loss function correlated to <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{a}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{a}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is only characterized by <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\rho\sqrt{A_{1}^{t}+A_{2}^{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\rho\sqrt{A_{1}^{t}+A_{2}^{t}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span>Problem Solution</h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">With Lyapunov optimization techniques and the derived upper bound, the long-term optimization problem <span id="S5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">P1</span> is transformed into a series of instantaneous optimization problems across all communication rounds. And each instantaneous optimization problem in a communication round is decomposed into two subproblems which can be individually solved. <span id="S5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The solving process of <span id="S5.p1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">P1</span> is presented in Figure <a href="#S5.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ 5 Problem Solution ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.F3" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.12930v1/Figure/flowchart.png" id="S5.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:234/111;" width="234" height="111" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 3: </span><span id="S5.F3.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Solving process of P1 to obtain <math id="S5.F3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(\bm{a}^{t*},\bm{B}^{t*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝒂</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000">∗</mo></mrow></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝑩</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000">∗</mo></mrow></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bm{a}^{t*},\bm{B}^{t*})</annotation></semantics></math> within the JCSBA algorithm.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="S5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.1 </span>Problem Transformation</h3>

<div id="S5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the long-term constraint <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">C5</span>, we firstly define a virtual queue as
<math id="S5.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{t}_{k}=\max\{Q^{t-1}_{k}-q^{t-1}_{k},0\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{t}_{k}=\max\{Q^{t-1}_{k}-q^{t-1}_{k},0\}.</annotation></semantics></math>
Equivalent to <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">C5</span>, the mean stability of the virtual queue is written by</p>
<table id="S5.E29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E29.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\textbf{C5}^{\prime}\textbf{:}\lim_{T\rightarrow+\infty}\frac{|Q^{T}_{k}|}{T}=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">C5</mtext><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">:</mtext><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textbf{C5}^{\prime}\textbf{:}\lim_{T\rightarrow+\infty}\frac{|Q^{T}_{k}|}{T}=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">With <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(\bm{\theta}^{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\bm{\theta}^{T})</annotation></semantics></math> minus a constant term <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(\bm{\theta}^{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\bm{\theta}^{0})</annotation></semantics></math> acting the new objective function, we obtain a equivalent optimization problem as</p>
<table id="S5.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\textbf{ P2: }\min_{\{(\bm{a}^{t},\bm{B}^{t})|t\}}\lim_{T\rightarrow+\infty}\sum^{T}_{t=1}(H(\bm{\theta}^{t})-H(\bm{\theta}^{t-1}))," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">P2: </mtext><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></munder><munder><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\textbf{ P2: }\min_{\{(\bm{a}^{t},\bm{B}^{t})|t\}}\lim_{T\rightarrow+\infty}\sum^{T}_{t=1}(H(\bm{\theta}^{t})-H(\bm{\theta}^{t-1})),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.E30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\kern 5.0pt{\rm s.t.}\quad\textbf{C1}\sim\textbf{C4},\ \textbf{C5}^{\prime}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">C1</mtext><mo>∼</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">C4</mtext></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">C5</mtext><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\kern 5.0pt{\rm s.t.}\quad\textbf{C1}\sim\textbf{C4},\ \textbf{C5}^{\prime}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">P2</span> is a standard structure for Lyapunov optimization. With Lyapunov optimization techniques <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">38</a>]</cite>, the pertubed Lyapunov function and the Laypunov drift-plus-penalty function are respectively
<math id="S5.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{t}=\frac{1}{2}\sum^{K}_{k=1}(Q_{k}^{t})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{t}=\frac{1}{2}\sum^{K}_{k=1}(Q_{k}^{t})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S5.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{t}_{V}=\mathbb{E}\{(\Delta^{t+1})^{2}-(\Delta^{t})^{2}+V(H(\bm{\theta}^{t})-H(\bm{\theta}^{t-1}))\ |\ Q_{k}^{t}\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em">|</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{t}_{V}=\mathbb{E}\{(\Delta^{t+1})^{2}-(\Delta^{t})^{2}+V(H(\bm{\theta}^{t})-H(\bm{\theta}^{t-1}))\ |\ Q_{k}^{t}\}.</annotation></semantics></math>
Substituting the upper bound of <span id="S5.SS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem <a href="#S4.EGx4" title="Theorem 2. ‣ 4.2 Main Results ‣ 4 MFL Performance Analysis ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></span>, utilizing <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\max{x,0})^{2}\leq x^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\max{x,0})^{2}\leq x^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and enlarging <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(q_{k}^{t})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(q_{k}^{t})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> into a positive constant <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can derive an upper bound of <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{V}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{V}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> as</p>
<table id="S5.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.E31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta_{V}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta_{V}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E31.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\sum^{K}_{k=1}[(\max\{Q_{k}^{t}-q_{k}^{t},0\})^{2}-(Q_{k}^{t})^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\sum^{K}_{k=1}[(\max\{Q_{k}^{t}-q_{k}^{t},0\})^{2}-(Q_{k}^{t})^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad-\frac{2\eta-\gamma\eta^{2}}{2}\sum_{m=1}^{M}\|\nabla H(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})\|^{2}+V\eta\rho\sqrt{A_{1}^{t}+A_{2}^{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mi>V</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>ρ</mi><msqrt><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad-\frac{2\eta-\gamma\eta^{2}}{2}\sum_{m=1}^{M}\|\nabla H(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})\|^{2}+V\eta\rho\sqrt{A_{1}^{t}+A_{2}^{t}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{2}\sum^{K}_{k=1}[(q_{k}^{t})^{2}-2Q_{k}^{t}q_{k}^{t}]-\frac{2\eta-\gamma\eta^{2}}{2}\sum_{m=1}^{M}\|\nabla H(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{2}\sum^{K}_{k=1}[(q_{k}^{t})^{2}-2Q_{k}^{t}q_{k}^{t}]-\frac{2\eta-\gamma\eta^{2}}{2}\sum_{m=1}^{M}\|\nabla H(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+V\eta\rho\sqrt{A_{1}^{t}+A_{2}^{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+V\eta\rho\sqrt{A_{1}^{t}+A_{2}^{t}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\Big(-\sum^{K}_{k=1}Q_{k}^{t}q_{k}^{t}+V\eta\rho\sqrt{A_{1}^{t}+A_{2}^{t}}+C_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mi>V</mi><mi>η</mi><mi>ρ</mi><msqrt><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\Big(-\sum^{K}_{k=1}Q_{k}^{t}q_{k}^{t}+V\eta\rho\sqrt{A_{1}^{t}+A_{2}^{t}}+C_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad-\frac{2\eta-\gamma\eta^{2}}{2}\sum_{m=1}^{M}\|\nabla H(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})\|^{2}\Big)\triangleq J_{0}(\bm{a}^{t},\bm{B}^{t})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo><mo>≜</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad-\frac{2\eta-\gamma\eta^{2}}{2}\sum_{m=1}^{M}\|\nabla H(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})\|^{2}\Big)\triangleq J_{0}(\bm{a}^{t},\bm{B}^{t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Setting <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{0}(\bm{a}^{t},\bm{B}^{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{0}(\bm{a}^{t},\bm{B}^{t})</annotation></semantics></math> as the objective function, we can find <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{0}-\frac{2\eta-\gamma\eta^{2}}{2}\sum_{m=1}^{M}\|\nabla H(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{0}-\frac{2\eta-\gamma\eta^{2}}{2}\sum_{m=1}^{M}\|\nabla H(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are unrelated to <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{a}^{t},\bm{B}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{a}^{t},\bm{B}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. Omitting the above two terms and <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{k}^{t}E^{\rm add}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>add</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{k}^{t}E^{\rm add}</annotation></semantics></math>, and substituting <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{k}^{t}=E^{\rm add}-a_{k}^{t}(e_{k}^{t,{\rm com}}+e_{k}^{{\rm cmp}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>add</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>com</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>cmp</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{k}^{t}=E^{\rm add}-a_{k}^{t}(e_{k}^{t,{\rm com}}+e_{k}^{{\rm cmp}})</annotation></semantics></math> into <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>J</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can formulate a transformed optimization problem as</p>
<table id="S5.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="S5.Ex13.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_bold">P3:</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\min_{\bm{a}^{t},\bm{B}^{t}}\Big(J_{1}(\bm{a}^{t},\bm{B}^{t})=V\eta\rho\sqrt{A_{1}^{t}+A_{2}^{t}}-\sum^{K}_{k=1}Q_{k}^{t}q_{k}^{t}\Big)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\min_{\bm{a}^{t},\bm{B}^{t}}\Big(J_{1}(\bm{a}^{t},\bm{B}^{t})=V\eta\rho\sqrt{A_{1}^{t}+A_{2}^{t}}-\sum^{K}_{k=1}Q_{k}^{t}q_{k}^{t}\Big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.E32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\rm s.t.}\kern 5.0pt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\rm s.t.}\kern 5.0pt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E32.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\textbf{C1}\sim\textbf{C4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">C1</mtext><mo>∼</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">C4</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\textbf{C1}\sim\textbf{C4}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Despite an instantaneous optimization problem in the <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>-th communication round, <span id="S5.SS1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">P3</span> is still mixed integer nonlinear programming (MINLP), which needs further decomposition to solve.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.2 </span>Problem Decomposition</h3>

<div id="S5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">According to Tammer decomposition <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>]</cite>, a equivalent optimization problem is</p>
<table id="S5.E33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S5.E33X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E33X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\textbf{ P4: }\min_{\bm{a}^{t}}\left(\min_{\bm{B}^{t}}J_{1}(\bm{a}^{t},\bm{B}^{t})\right),\qquad\textbf{ s.t.}\kern 5.0pt\textbf{C1}\sim\textbf{C4}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">P4: </mtext><mi>min</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>min</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></msub><mi>J</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑩</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold"> s.t.</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">C1</mtext><mo>∼</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">C4</mtext><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\textbf{ P4: }\min_{\bm{a}^{t}}\left(\min_{\bm{B}^{t}}J_{1}(\bm{a}^{t},\bm{B}^{t})\right),\qquad\textbf{ s.t.}\kern 5.0pt\textbf{C1}\sim\textbf{C4}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">The outer combinatorial subproblem with respect to <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{a}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{a}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="S5.E34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S5.E34X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E34X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\textbf{ P4.1: }\min_{\bm{a}^{t}}J_{2}(\bm{a}^{t}),\qquad\textbf{ s.t.}\kern 5.0pt\textbf{C1},\textbf{C3},\textbf{C4}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">P4.1: </mtext><mi>min</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></msub><mi>J</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold"> s.t.</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">C1</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">C3</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">C4</mtext><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\textbf{ P4.1: }\min_{\bm{a}^{t}}J_{2}(\bm{a}^{t}),\qquad\textbf{ s.t.}\kern 5.0pt\textbf{C1},\textbf{C3},\textbf{C4}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">The objective function of <span id="S5.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">P4.1</span> is defined by <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="J_{2}(\bm{a}^{t})\triangleq J_{1}(\bm{a}^{t},\bm{B}^{t*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≜</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝑩</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{2}(\bm{a}^{t})\triangleq J_{1}(\bm{a}^{t},\bm{B}^{t*})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{B}^{t*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑩</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{B}^{t*}</annotation></semantics></math> is the optimal point of the inner continuous problem, which can be expressed by</p>
<table id="S5.E35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S5.E35X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E35X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\textbf{ P4.2: }\min_{\bm{B}^{t}}J_{3}(\bm{B}^{t}),\qquad\textbf{ s.t.}\kern 5.0pt\textbf{C2}\sim\textbf{C4}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">P4.2: </mtext><mi>min</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></msub><mi>J</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑩</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold"> s.t.</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">C2</mtext><mo>∼</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">C4</mtext><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\textbf{ P4.2: }\min_{\bm{B}^{t}}J_{3}(\bm{B}^{t}),\qquad\textbf{ s.t.}\kern 5.0pt\textbf{C2}\sim\textbf{C4},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{3}(\bm{B}^{t})=\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}^{t}}\frac{Q_{k}^{t}p\Gamma_{k}}{B_{k}^{t}\log_{2}(1+\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{B_{k}^{t}N_{0}})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{3}(\bm{B}^{t})=\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}^{t}}\frac{Q_{k}^{t}p\Gamma_{k}}{B_{k}^{t}\log_{2}(1+\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{B_{k}^{t}N_{0}})}</annotation></semantics></math> comes from <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>J</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> omitting constant and terms corresponding to <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{a}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{a}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> since <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{a}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{a}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is fixed in <span id="S5.SS2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">P4.2</span>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.3 </span>Continuous Subproblem</h3>

<div id="S5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">With the given <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{a}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{a}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, bandwidth should be allocated to only participating clients. Hence, <span id="S5.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">P4.2</span> is rewritten as</p>
<table id="S5.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="S5.Ex14.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_bold">P4.2</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex14.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{}^{\prime}\textbf{: }\min_{\bm{B}^{t}}\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}^{t}}\frac{Q_{k}^{t}p\Gamma_{k}}{B_{k}^{t}\log_{2}(1+\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{B_{k}^{t}N_{0}})}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">: </mtext><mi>min</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>𝑩</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{}^{\prime}\textbf{: }\min_{\bm{B}^{t}}\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}^{t}}\frac{Q_{k}^{t}p\Gamma_{k}}{B_{k}^{t}\log_{2}(1+\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{B_{k}^{t}N_{0}})},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.E36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\rm s.t.}\kern 5.0pt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\rm s.t.}\kern 5.0pt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E36.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\textbf{C2}^{\prime}\textbf{:}\ B_{k}^{t}\leq 0,\quad\forall k\in\mathcal{K}^{t}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">C2</mtext><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">:</mtext><mi>B</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\textbf{C2}^{\prime}\textbf{:}\ B_{k}^{t}\leq 0,\quad\forall k\in\mathcal{K}^{t},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\textbf{C3}^{\prime}\textbf{:}\ \sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}^{t}}B_{k}^{t}=B^{\max}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">C3</mtext><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">:</mtext><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>B</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>max</mi></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\textbf{C3}^{\prime}\textbf{:}\ \sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}^{t}}B_{k}^{t}=B^{\max},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\textbf{C4}^{\prime}\textbf{:}\ \frac{\Gamma_{k}}{B_{k}^{t}\log_{2}(1+\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{B_{k}^{t}N_{0}})}+\frac{D_{k}\Phi_{k}}{f}\leq\tau^{\max},\ \forall k\in\mathcal{K}^{t}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">C4</mtext><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">:</mtext><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mi>f</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≤</mo><mi>τ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>max</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\textbf{C4}^{\prime}\textbf{:}\ \frac{\Gamma_{k}}{B_{k}^{t}\log_{2}(1+\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{B_{k}^{t}N_{0}})}+\frac{D_{k}\Phi_{k}}{f}\leq\tau^{\max},\ \forall k\in\mathcal{K}^{t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Compared to the bandwidth allocation problem in wirless FL, there are different energy queue lengths and computation latency in <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textbf{P4.2}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">P4.2</mtext><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textbf{P4.2}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Fortunately, we can prove that <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textbf{P4.2}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">P4.2</mtext><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textbf{P4.2}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is a convex problem and utilize Karush-Kuhn-Tucker (KKT) conditions to obtain the optimal bandwidth vector.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The first-order derivative and the second-order derivative of objective function of <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textbf{P4.2}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">P4.2</mtext><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textbf{P4.2}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{k}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{k}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> are expressed by</p>
<table id="S5.E37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial J_{3}}{\partial B_{k}^{t}}=Q_{k}^{t}p\Gamma_{k}(\ln 2)\frac{\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{ph_{k}^{t}+B_{k}^{t}N_{0}}-\ln(1+\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{B_{k}^{t}N_{0}})}{(B_{k}^{t})^{2}\ln^{2}(1+\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{B_{k}^{t}N_{0}})}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ln</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial J_{3}}{\partial B_{k}^{t}}=Q_{k}^{t}p\Gamma_{k}(\ln 2)\frac{\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{ph_{k}^{t}+B_{k}^{t}N_{0}}-\ln(1+\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{B_{k}^{t}N_{0}})}{(B_{k}^{t})^{2}\ln^{2}(1+\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{B_{k}^{t}N_{0}})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S5.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial^{2}J_{3}}{(\partial B_{k}^{t})^{2}}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>J</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial^{2}J_{3}}{(\partial B_{k}^{t})^{2}}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex17.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{Q_{k}^{t}p\Gamma_{k}(\ln 2)}{(B_{k}^{t})^{2}\ln^{3}(1+\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{B_{k}^{t}N_{0}})}\left[\frac{p^{2}(h_{k}^{t})^{2}\ln(1+\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{B_{k}^{t}N_{0}})}{(ph_{k}^{t}+B_{k}^{t}N_{0})^{2}}\right." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ln</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{Q_{k}^{t}p\Gamma_{k}(\ln 2)}{(B_{k}^{t})^{2}\ln^{3}(1+\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{B_{k}^{t}N_{0}})}\left[\frac{p^{2}(h_{k}^{t})^{2}\ln(1+\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{B_{k}^{t}N_{0}})}{(ph_{k}^{t}+B_{k}^{t}N_{0})^{2}}\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.E38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E38.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\left.+2\left(\ln(1+\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{B_{k}^{t}N_{0}})-\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{B_{k}^{t}N_{0}+ph_{k}^{t}}\right)^{2}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>ln</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left.+2\left(\ln(1+\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{B_{k}^{t}N_{0}})-\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{B_{k}^{t}N_{0}+ph_{k}^{t}}\right)^{2}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">It is obvious that <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial^{2}J_{3}}{(\partial B_{k}^{t})^{2}}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>J</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial^{2}J_{3}}{(\partial B_{k}^{t})^{2}}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Similarly, we can prove that the function on the left side of <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textbf{C4}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">C4</mtext><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textbf{C4}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is convex. <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textbf{C2}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">C2</mtext><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textbf{C2}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is a convex set and <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textbf{C3}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">C3</mtext><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textbf{C3}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is a linear constraint. As such, <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textbf{P4.2}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">P4.2</mtext><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textbf{P4.2}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is a convex optimization problem. Its Lagrange function is written by
<math id="S5.SS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm La}=\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}^{t}}\!\!\frac{Q_{k}^{t}p\Gamma_{k}}{B_{k}^{t}\log_{2}(1+\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{B_{k}^{t}N_{0}})}-\!\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}^{t}}\!\lambda_{2,k}B_{k}^{t}+\kappa(B^{\max}\!\!-\!\!\!\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}^{t}}\!B_{i}^{t})+\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}^{t}}\lambda_{4,k}(\frac{\Gamma_{k}}{B_{k}^{t}\log_{2}(1+\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{B_{k}^{t}N_{0}})}+\frac{D_{k}\Phi_{k}}{f}-\tau^{\max})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>La</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="0.026em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.026em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mi>max</mi></msup><mpadded style="width:0.462em;" width="0.462em"><mo>−</mo></mpadded><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mi>f</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mi>max</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm La}=\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}^{t}}\!\!\frac{Q_{k}^{t}p\Gamma_{k}}{B_{k}^{t}\log_{2}(1+\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{B_{k}^{t}N_{0}})}-\!\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}^{t}}\!\lambda_{2,k}B_{k}^{t}+\kappa(B^{\max}\!\!-\!\!\!\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}^{t}}\!B_{i}^{t})+\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}^{t}}\lambda_{4,k}(\frac{\Gamma_{k}}{B_{k}^{t}\log_{2}(1+\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{B_{k}^{t}N_{0}})}+\frac{D_{k}\Phi_{k}}{f}-\tau^{\max}).</annotation></semantics></math>
Thus the KKT conditions are given by
<span id="S5.SS3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text"></span></p>
<table id="S5.E39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E39.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\left\{\begin{aligned} &amp;\lambda_{2,k},\lambda_{4,k}\geq 0,\hskip 9.24994pt\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}^{t}}B_{k}^{t}-B^{\max}=0,\\
&amp;-B_{k}^{t}\leq 0,\hskip 9.24994pt\frac{\Gamma_{k}}{B_{k}^{t}\log_{2}(1+\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{B_{k}^{t}N_{0}})}\leq\tau^{\max}-\frac{D_{k}\Phi_{k}}{f},\\
&amp;\lambda_{2,k}B_{k}^{t}=0,\kern 4.62497pt\lambda_{4,k}\big(\frac{\Gamma_{k}}{B_{k}^{t}\log_{2}(1+\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{B_{k}^{t}N_{0}})}+\frac{D_{k}\Phi_{k}}{f}-\tau^{\max}\big)=0,\\
&amp;(Q_{k}^{t}p\Gamma_{k}+\lambda_{4,k}\Gamma_{k})\frac{\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{ph_{k}^{t}+B_{k}^{t}N_{0}}-\ln(1+\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{B_{k}^{t}N_{0}})}{\frac{1}{\ln 2}(B_{k}^{t})^{2}\ln^{2}(1+\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{B_{k}^{t}N_{0}})}-\lambda_{2,k}\!-\kappa=0.\end{aligned}\right." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">λ</mi><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">λ</mi><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">4</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">≥</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.930em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒦</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msup></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">B</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">B</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">max</mi></msup></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">B</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msup><mo mathsize="0.900em">≤</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="1.097em">,</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">B</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">h</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">B</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo mathsize="0.900em">≤</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">τ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">max</mi></msup><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">D</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi></msub></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">f</mi></mfrac><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">λ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi></mrow></msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">B</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msup><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.627em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">λ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">4</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">B</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">h</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">B</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">D</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi></msub></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">f</mi></mfrac><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">τ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">max</mi></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">Q</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi></msub></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">λ</mi><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">4</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">h</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">h</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">B</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">h</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">B</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">B</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ln</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">h</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">B</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">λ</mi><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">κ</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{\begin{aligned} &amp;\lambda_{2,k},\lambda_{4,k}\geq 0,\hskip 9.24994pt\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}^{t}}B_{k}^{t}-B^{\max}=0,\\
&amp;-B_{k}^{t}\leq 0,\hskip 9.24994pt\frac{\Gamma_{k}}{B_{k}^{t}\log_{2}(1+\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{B_{k}^{t}N_{0}})}\leq\tau^{\max}-\frac{D_{k}\Phi_{k}}{f},\\
&amp;\lambda_{2,k}B_{k}^{t}=0,\kern 4.62497pt\lambda_{4,k}\big(\frac{\Gamma_{k}}{B_{k}^{t}\log_{2}(1+\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{B_{k}^{t}N_{0}})}+\frac{D_{k}\Phi_{k}}{f}-\tau^{\max}\big)=0,\\
&amp;(Q_{k}^{t}p\Gamma_{k}+\lambda_{4,k}\Gamma_{k})\frac{\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{ph_{k}^{t}+B_{k}^{t}N_{0}}-\ln(1+\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{B_{k}^{t}N_{0}})}{\frac{1}{\ln 2}(B_{k}^{t})^{2}\ln^{2}(1+\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{B_{k}^{t}N_{0}})}-\lambda_{2,k}\!-\kappa=0.\end{aligned}\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p2.3" class="ltx_p">It is obvious that the allocated bandwidth of each participating client <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> is large than 0. Hence, we derive <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{2,k}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{2,k}=0</annotation></semantics></math> from the complementary relaxation condition <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{2,k}B_{k}^{t}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{2,k}B_{k}^{t}=0</annotation></semantics></math>. The KKT conditions, then, can be transformed into
<span id="S5.SS3.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text"></span></p>
<table id="S5.E40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E40.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\left\{\begin{aligned} &amp;\lambda_{4,k}\geq 0,\hskip 9.24994pt\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}^{t}}B_{k}^{t}-B^{\max}=0,\hskip 9.24994ptB_{k}^{t}&gt;0,\\
&amp;\textbf{In1:}\ \frac{\Gamma_{k}}{B_{k}^{t}\log_{2}(1+\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{B_{k}^{t}N_{0}})}\leq\tau^{\max}-\frac{D_{k}\Phi_{k}}{f},\\
&amp;\textbf{E1:}\ \lambda_{4,k}\big(\frac{\Gamma_{k}}{B_{k}^{t}\log_{2}(1+\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{B_{k}^{t}N_{0}})}+\frac{D_{k}\Phi_{k}}{f}-\tau^{\max}\big)=0,\\
&amp;\textbf{E2:}\ (Q_{k}^{t}p\Gamma_{k}+\lambda_{4,k}\Gamma_{k})\frac{\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{ph_{k}^{t}+B_{k}^{t}N_{0}}-\ln(1+\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{B_{k}^{t}N_{0}})}{\frac{1}{\ln 2}(B_{k}^{t})^{2}\ln^{2}(1+\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{B_{k}^{t}N_{0}})}=\kappa.\end{aligned}\right." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">λ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">4</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">≥</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.930em">,</mo><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒦</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">B</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msup><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">B</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">max</mi></msup><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="1.097em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">B</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msup><mo mathsize="0.900em">&gt;</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathsize="0.900em">In1:</mtext><mfrac><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">B</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">h</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">B</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo mathsize="0.900em">≤</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">τ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">max</mi></msup><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">D</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi></msub></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">f</mi></mfrac><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathsize="0.900em">E1:</mtext><mi mathsize="0.900em">λ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">4</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">B</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">h</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">B</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">D</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi></msub></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">f</mi></mfrac><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">τ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">max</mi></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathsize="0.900em">E2:</mtext><mo lspace="0.460em" maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">Q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">p</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">λ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">4</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi></mrow></msub><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">h</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">h</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">B</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">h</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">B</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">B</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ln</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">h</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">B</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{\begin{aligned} &amp;\lambda_{4,k}\geq 0,\hskip 9.24994pt\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}^{t}}B_{k}^{t}-B^{\max}=0,\hskip 9.24994ptB_{k}^{t}&gt;0,\\
&amp;\textbf{In1:}\ \frac{\Gamma_{k}}{B_{k}^{t}\log_{2}(1+\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{B_{k}^{t}N_{0}})}\leq\tau^{\max}-\frac{D_{k}\Phi_{k}}{f},\\
&amp;\textbf{E1:}\ \lambda_{4,k}\big(\frac{\Gamma_{k}}{B_{k}^{t}\log_{2}(1+\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{B_{k}^{t}N_{0}})}+\frac{D_{k}\Phi_{k}}{f}-\tau^{\max}\big)=0,\\
&amp;\textbf{E2:}\ (Q_{k}^{t}p\Gamma_{k}+\lambda_{4,k}\Gamma_{k})\frac{\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{ph_{k}^{t}+B_{k}^{t}N_{0}}-\ln(1+\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{B_{k}^{t}N_{0}})}{\frac{1}{\ln 2}(B_{k}^{t})^{2}\ln^{2}(1+\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{B_{k}^{t}N_{0}})}=\kappa.\end{aligned}\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p2.4" class="ltx_p">We observe that <span id="S5.SS3.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">In1</span> has a equivalent inequality <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{k}^{t}\geq B_{k}^{t,\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>≥</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{k}^{t}\geq B_{k}^{t,\min}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{k}^{t,\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{k}^{t,\min}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies</p>
<table id="S5.E41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\Gamma_{k}}{B_{k}^{t,\min}\log_{2}(1+\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{B_{k}^{t,\min}N_{0}})}=\tau^{\max}-\frac{D_{k}\Phi_{k}}{f}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mi>max</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mi>f</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\Gamma_{k}}{B_{k}^{t,\min}\log_{2}(1+\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{B_{k}^{t,\min}N_{0}})}=\tau^{\max}-\frac{D_{k}\Phi_{k}}{f}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p2.5" class="ltx_p">Due to <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial J_{3}}{\partial B_{k}^{t}}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial J_{3}}{\partial B_{k}^{t}}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, the function in the left side of (<a href="#S5.E41" title="In 5.3 Continuous Subproblem ‣ 5 Problem Solution ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">41</span></a>), which is equal to the objective function in <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textbf{P4.2}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">P4.2</mtext><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textbf{P4.2}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> divided by <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{J_{3}}{Q_{k}^{t}p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><msub><mi>J</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{J_{3}}{Q_{k}^{t}p}</annotation></semantics></math>, monotonically increases with bandwidth increasing. Hence, we deduce that (<a href="#S5.E41" title="In 5.3 Continuous Subproblem ‣ 5 Problem Solution ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">41</span></a>) has a unique solution <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{k}^{t,\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{k}^{t,\min}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{k}^{t}\geq B_{k}^{t,\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>≥</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{k}^{t}\geq B_{k}^{t,\min}</annotation></semantics></math> is a necessary and sufficient condition of <span id="S5.SS3.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">In1</span>. As a transcendental equation, (<a href="#S5.E41" title="In 5.3 Continuous Subproblem ‣ 5 Problem Solution ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">41</span></a>) relies on numerical methods such as the Newton iteration method to solve. After obtaining <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{k}^{t,\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{k}^{t,\min}</annotation></semantics></math>, the feasibility of <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{a}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{a}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> can be judged by</p>
<table id="S5.E42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}^{t}}B_{k}^{t,\min}\leq B^{\max}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mi>max</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}^{t}}B_{k}^{t,\min}\leq B^{\max}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Unsatisfied (<a href="#S5.E42" title="In 5.3 Continuous Subproblem ‣ 5 Problem Solution ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">42</span></a>) suggests that given <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{a}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{a}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is infeasible. If (<a href="#S5.E42" title="In 5.3 Continuous Subproblem ‣ 5 Problem Solution ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">42</span></a>) holds with equality, we can prove that the optimal bandwidth for <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\mathcal{K}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\mathcal{K}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="B_{k}^{t*}=B_{k}^{t,\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>B</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{k}^{t*}=B_{k}^{t,\min}</annotation></semantics></math>. Otherwise, (<a href="#S5.E42" title="In 5.3 Continuous Subproblem ‣ 5 Problem Solution ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">42</span></a>) is loose, and then we define <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{k}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>κ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{k}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> by
<math id="S5.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{k}^{t}\triangleq Q_{k}^{t}p\Gamma_{k}\cdot\frac{\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{ph_{k}^{t}+B_{k}^{t,\min}N_{0}}-\ln(1+\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{B_{k}^{t,\min}N_{0}})}{\frac{1}{\ln 2}(B_{k}^{t,\min})^{2}\ln^{2}(1+\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{B_{k}^{t,\min}N_{0}})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>κ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>≜</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ln</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{k}^{t}\triangleq Q_{k}^{t}p\Gamma_{k}\cdot\frac{\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{ph_{k}^{t}+B_{k}^{t,\min}N_{0}}-\ln(1+\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{B_{k}^{t,\min}N_{0}})}{\frac{1}{\ln 2}(B_{k}^{t,\min})^{2}\ln^{2}(1+\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{B_{k}^{t,\min}N_{0}})}</annotation></semantics></math>
We can easily prove <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{k}^{t}&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>κ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{k}^{t}&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Without loss of generality, arrange <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{k}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>κ</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{k}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> of participating clients in ascending order as <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa^{t}_{i_{1}}\leq\kappa^{t}_{i_{2}}\leq\kappa^{t}_{i_{3}}\leq\cdots\leq\kappa^{t}_{i_{\varkappa}}&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>κ</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>κ</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>κ</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><msubsup><mi>κ</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>ϰ</mi></msub><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa^{t}_{i_{1}}\leq\kappa^{t}_{i_{2}}\leq\kappa^{t}_{i_{3}}\leq\cdots\leq\kappa^{t}_{i_{\varkappa}}&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varkappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varkappa</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of clients in <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. According to the function in the left side of <span id="S5.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">E2</span> monotonically increasing with <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{k}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{k}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{4,k}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{4,k}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, feasible <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa\geq\kappa_{i_{1}}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>≥</mo><msubsup><mi>κ</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa\geq\kappa_{i_{1}}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequently, the value of <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> is either between <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{i_{j}}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>κ</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{i_{j}}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{i_{j+1}}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>κ</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{i_{j+1}}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> or beyond <math id="S5.SS3.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa^{t}_{i_{\varkappa}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>κ</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>ϰ</mi></msub><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa^{t}_{i_{\varkappa}}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e.</p>
<table id="S5.E43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E43.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\left\{\begin{aligned} &amp;\kappa=\kappa_{i_{1}};\\
&amp;\kappa\in(\kappa_{i_{j}},\kappa_{i_{j+1}}],\quad j=1,2,\cdots,\varkappa-1;\\
&amp;\kappa\in(\kappa_{i_{\varkappa}},+\infty).\end{aligned}\right." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>κ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>κ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>ϰ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>;</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>ϰ</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\{\begin{aligned} &amp;\kappa=\kappa_{i_{1}};\\
&amp;\kappa\in(\kappa_{i_{j}},\kappa_{i_{j+1}}],\quad j=1,2,\cdots,\varkappa-1;\\
&amp;\kappa\in(\kappa_{i_{\varkappa}},+\infty).\end{aligned}\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">If <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa=\kappa_{i_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa=\kappa_{i_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can easily derive the same solution as strictly satisfied (<a href="#S5.E42" title="In 5.3 Continuous Subproblem ‣ 5 Problem Solution ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">42</span></a>). And we directly take <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa\in(\kappa_{i_{j}},\kappa_{i_{j+1}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa\in(\kappa_{i_{j}},\kappa_{i_{j+1}}]</annotation></semantics></math> into consideration. For client <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=i_{1},\cdots,i_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=i_{1},\cdots,i_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can deduce <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{4,k}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{4,k}=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{k}^{t}&gt;B_{k}^{t,\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{k}^{t}&gt;B_{k}^{t,\min}</annotation></semantics></math> from <span id="S5.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">E1</span> and <span id="S5.SS3.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">E2</span>. Similar to (<a href="#S5.E41" title="In 5.3 Continuous Subproblem ‣ 5 Problem Solution ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">41</span></a>), we firstly solve the boundary bandwidth <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{k,{j+1}}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{k,{j+1}}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying</p>
<table id="S5.E44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{k}^{t}p\Gamma_{k}\frac{\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{ph_{k}^{t}+B_{k,{j+1}}^{t}N_{0}}-\ln(1+\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{B_{k,{j+1}}^{t}N_{0}})}{\frac{1}{\ln 2}(B_{k,{j+1}}^{t})^{2}\ln^{2}(1+\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{B_{k,{j+1}}^{t}N_{0}})}=\kappa_{i_{j+1}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ln</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{k}^{t}p\Gamma_{k}\frac{\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{ph_{k}^{t}+B_{k,{j+1}}^{t}N_{0}}-\ln(1+\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{B_{k,{j+1}}^{t}N_{0}})}{\frac{1}{\ln 2}(B_{k,{j+1}}^{t})^{2}\ln^{2}(1+\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{B_{k,{j+1}}^{t}N_{0}})}=\kappa_{i_{j+1}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Furthermore, due to <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{4,k}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{4,k}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for <span id="S5.SS3.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">E1</span> and <span id="S5.SS3.p4.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">E2</span>, client <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=i_{j+1},i_{j+2},\cdots,i_{\varkappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>ϰ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=i_{j+1},i_{j+2},\cdots,i_{\varkappa}</annotation></semantics></math> has <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="B_{k}^{t*}=B_{k}^{t,\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>B</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{k}^{t*}=B_{k}^{t,\min}</annotation></semantics></math>. As thus, a prerequisite inequality is formulated as</p>
<table id="S5.E45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E45.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\textbf{Pre:}\sum_{k=i_{1}}^{i_{j}}B^{t}_{k,j+1}+\sum_{k=i_{j+1}}^{i_{\varkappa}}B_{k}^{t,\min}\geq B^{\max}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">Pre:</mtext><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msup><mi>B</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>ϰ</mi></msub></msup><mi>B</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow></msup><mo>≥</mo><mi>B</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>max</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textbf{Pre:}\sum_{k=i_{1}}^{i_{j}}B^{t}_{k,j+1}+\sum_{k=i_{j+1}}^{i_{\varkappa}}B_{k}^{t,\min}\geq B^{\max}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p4.3" class="ltx_p">If <span id="S5.SS3.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pre</span> is not satisfied on <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\kappa_{i_{j}},\kappa_{i_{j+1}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\kappa_{i_{j}},\kappa_{i_{j+1}}]</annotation></semantics></math>, the next interval <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\kappa_{i_{j+1}},\kappa_{i_{j+2}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\kappa_{i_{j+1}},\kappa_{i_{j+2}}]</annotation></semantics></math> will be considered till <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\kappa_{i_{\varkappa}},+\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>ϰ</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\kappa_{i_{\varkappa}},+\infty)</annotation></semantics></math>. Without loss of generality, we suppose that <span id="S5.SS3.p4.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pre</span> holds on <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\kappa_{i_{j}},\kappa_{i_{j+1}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\kappa_{i_{j}},\kappa_{i_{j+1}}]</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, the equation of <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>κ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is formulated by</p>
<table id="S5.E46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E46.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sum_{k=i_{1}}^{i_{j}}B^{t*}_{k}(\kappa^{*})+\sum_{k=i_{j+1}}^{i_{\varkappa}}B_{k}^{t,\min}=B^{\max}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></munderover><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>ϰ</mi></msub></munderover><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mi>max</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=i_{1}}^{i_{j}}B^{t*}_{k}(\kappa^{*})+\sum_{k=i_{j+1}}^{i_{\varkappa}}B_{k}^{t,\min}=B^{\max}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(46)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p4.4" class="ltx_p">Substituting <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{4,k}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{4,k}=0</annotation></semantics></math> into <span id="S5.SS3.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">E2</span>, the relation between <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m16" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="B^{t*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{t*}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>κ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> for client <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=i_{1},\cdots,i_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=i_{1},\cdots,i_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> is expressed by</p>
<table id="S5.E47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{k}^{t}p\Gamma_{k}\frac{\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{ph_{k}^{t}+B_{k}^{t*}N_{0}}-\ln(1+\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{B_{k}^{t*}N_{0}})}{\frac{1}{\ln 2}(B_{k}^{t*})^{2}\ln^{2}(1+\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{B_{k}^{t*}N_{0}})}=\kappa^{*}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>h</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msup><mi>N</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msup><mi>N</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>ln</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msup><mi>N</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{k}^{t}p\Gamma_{k}\frac{\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{ph_{k}^{t}+B_{k}^{t*}N_{0}}-\ln(1+\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{B_{k}^{t*}N_{0}})}{\frac{1}{\ln 2}(B_{k}^{t*})^{2}\ln^{2}(1+\frac{ph_{k}^{t}}{B_{k}^{t*}N_{0}})}=\kappa^{*}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(47)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p4.5" class="ltx_p">Despite no closed-form function for <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m19" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="B_{k}^{t*}(\kappa^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{k}^{t*}(\kappa^{*})</annotation></semantics></math>, the Newton iteration method can be utilized since <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{dB_{k}^{t*}}{d\kappa^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>B</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{dB_{k}^{t*}}{d\kappa^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math> is equal to <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{\frac{d\kappa^{*}}{dB_{k}^{t*}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>B</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{\frac{d\kappa^{*}}{dB_{k}^{t*}}}</annotation></semantics></math> according to implicit differentiation of (<a href="#S5.E47" title="In 5.3 Continuous Subproblem ‣ 5 Problem Solution ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">47</span></a>), so that <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m22" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="B_{k}^{t*}(\kappa^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{k}^{t*}(\kappa^{*})</annotation></semantics></math> is solved for client <math id="S5.SS3.p4.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=i_{1},\cdots,i_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=i_{1},\cdots,i_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">If there is no <math id="S5.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\kappa_{i_{j}},\kappa_{i_{j+1}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\kappa_{i_{j}},\kappa_{i_{j+1}}]</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying <span id="S5.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pre</span>, <math id="S5.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\kappa_{i_{\varkappa}},+\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>ϰ</mi></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\kappa_{i_{\varkappa}},+\infty)</annotation></semantics></math> will finally be considered. And the corresponding formulation for client <math id="S5.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=i_{1},i_{2},\cdots,i_{\varkappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>ϰ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=i_{1},i_{2},\cdots,i_{\varkappa}</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="S5.E48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E48.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sum_{k=i_{1}}^{i_{\varkappa}}B^{t*}_{k}(\kappa^{*})=B^{\max}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>ϰ</mi></msub></munderover><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mi>max</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=i_{1}}^{i_{\varkappa}}B^{t*}_{k}(\kappa^{*})=B^{\max}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(48)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p5.2" class="ltx_p">Similar to (<a href="#S5.E46" title="In 5.3 Continuous Subproblem ‣ 5 Problem Solution ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">46</span></a>), (<a href="#S5.E48" title="In 5.3 Continuous Subproblem ‣ 5 Problem Solution ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">48</span></a>) can be solved by the Newton iteration method and implicit differentiation of (<a href="#S5.E47" title="In 5.3 Continuous Subproblem ‣ 5 Problem Solution ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">47</span></a>). To sum up, the optimal bandwidth for <math id="S5.SS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\mathcal{K}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\mathcal{K}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is (<a href="#S5.E49" title="In 5.3 Continuous Subproblem ‣ 5 Problem Solution ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">49</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.SS3.fig1" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<table id="S5.E49" class="ltx_equation ltx_figure_panel ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_figure_panel ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E49.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="B^{t*}_{k}=\left\{\begin{aligned} &amp;0\ {\rm for}\ k\in\mathcal{K}^{t},&{\rm(\ref{equation: bandwidth detect})\ is\ unsatisfied};\\
&amp;B_{k}^{t,\min}\ {\rm for}\ k\in\mathcal{K}^{t},&{\rm(\ref{equation: bandwidth detect})\ holds\ with\ equality};\\
&amp;B_{k}^{t,\min}\ {\rm for}\ k=i_{j+1},\cdots,i_{\varkappa};\ {\rm solve\,(\ref{eq4: bandwidth sum})\ and\ }\textbf{E2}\ {\rm for}\ k=i_{1},\cdots,i_{j},&{\rm(\ref{equation: bandwidth detect})\ is\ loose,\&gt;}\textbf{Pre}\ {\rm is\ satisfied};\\
&{\rm solve\ (\ref{eq4: bandwidth sum max})\ and\ }\textbf{E2}\ {\rm for}\ k\in\mathcal{K}^{t},&{\rm(\ref{equation: bandwidth detect})\ is\ loose,\ but\ }\textbf{Pre}\ {\rm is\ not\ satisfied}.\end{aligned}\right." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>for</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext><a href="#S5.E42" title="In 5.3 Continuous Subproblem ‣ 5 Problem Solution ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">42</span></a></mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>is</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>unsatisfied</mi></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>for</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext><a href="#S5.E42" title="In 5.3 Continuous Subproblem ‣ 5 Problem Solution ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">42</span></a></mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>holds</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>with</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>equality</mi></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>for</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>ϰ</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.667em">;</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>solve</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext><a href="#S5.E46" title="In 5.3 Continuous Subproblem ‣ 5 Problem Solution ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">46</span></a></mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>and</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">E2</mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>for</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext><a href="#S5.E42" title="In 5.3 Continuous Subproblem ‣ 5 Problem Solution ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">42</span></a></mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>is</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>loose</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.387em">,</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">Pre</mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>is</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>satisfied</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>solve</mi><mo lspace="0.500em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext><a href="#S5.E48" title="In 5.3 Continuous Subproblem ‣ 5 Problem Solution ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">48</span></a></mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>and</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">E2</mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>for</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext><a href="#S5.E42" title="In 5.3 Continuous Subproblem ‣ 5 Problem Solution ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">42</span></a></mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>is</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>loose</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi>but</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">Pre</mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>is</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>not</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>satisfied</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{t*}_{k}=\left\{\begin{aligned} &amp;0\ {\rm for}\ k\in\mathcal{K}^{t},&amp;{\rm(\ref{equation: bandwidth detect})\ is\ unsatisfied};\\
&amp;B_{k}^{t,\min}\ {\rm for}\ k\in\mathcal{K}^{t},&amp;{\rm(\ref{equation: bandwidth detect})\ holds\ with\ equality};\\
&amp;B_{k}^{t,\min}\ {\rm for}\ k=i_{j+1},\cdots,i_{\varkappa};\ {\rm solve\,(\ref{eq4: bandwidth sum})\ and\ }\textbf{E2}\ {\rm for}\ k=i_{1},\cdots,i_{j},&amp;{\rm(\ref{equation: bandwidth detect})\ is\ loose,\&gt;}\textbf{Pre}\ {\rm is\ satisfied};\\
&amp;{\rm solve\ (\ref{eq4: bandwidth sum max})\ and\ }\textbf{E2}\ {\rm for}\ k\in\mathcal{K}^{t},&amp;{\rm(\ref{equation: bandwidth detect})\ is\ loose,\ but\ }\textbf{Pre}\ {\rm is\ not\ satisfied}.\end{aligned}\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(49)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<p id="S5.SS3.fig1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_figure_panel"><span id="S5.SS3.fig1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_leader"><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:100%;height:1px;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></span></p></div></div>
</figure>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span>Immune Algorithm for Client Scheduling</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.4.1" class="ltx_listingline">
<span id="alg2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="alg2.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> </span><math id="alg2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=20,G=10,\mu=5,z=0.175" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">20</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">10</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">z</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0.175</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=20,G=10,\mu=5,z=0.175</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="alg2.4.2" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="alg2.4.2.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="alg2.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span> </span>optimal participation vector <math id="alg2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{a}^{t*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{a}^{t*}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="alg2.4.3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.4.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1</span></span>
            Initialize the set of <math id="alg2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> antibodies randomly as <math id="alg2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}^{0}=\{\bm{a}_{1}^{t,0},\bm{a}_{2}^{t,0},\cdots,\bm{a}_{S}^{t,0}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}^{0}=\{\bm{a}_{1}^{t,0},\bm{a}_{2}^{t,0},\cdots,\bm{a}_{S}^{t,0}\}</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="alg2.4.4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.4.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">2</span></span>
            <span id="alg2.4.4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="alg2.4.4.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="alg2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g=0,1,\cdots,G-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g=0,1,\cdots,G-1</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="alg2.4.4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.4.5" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.4.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">3</span></span>
            <span id="alg2.4.5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="alg2.4.5.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="alg2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=1,2,\cdots,S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=1,2,\cdots,S</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="alg2.4.5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.4.6" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.4.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">4</span></span>
            Compute <math id="alg2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm aff}({\bm{a}_{s}^{t,g}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>aff</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm aff}({\bm{a}_{s}^{t,g}})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="alg2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm con}(\bm{a}_{s}^{t,g})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>con</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm con}(\bm{a}_{s}^{t,g})</annotation></semantics></math> for antibody <math id="alg2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{a}_{s}^{t,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{a}_{s}^{t,g}</annotation></semantics></math> according to (<a href="#S5.E50" title="In 5.4 Combinatorial Subproblem ‣ 5 Problem Solution ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">50</span></a>) and (<a href="#S5.E51" title="In 5.4 Combinatorial Subproblem ‣ 5 Problem Solution ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">51</span></a>);
</div>
<div id="alg2.4.7" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.4.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">5</span></span>
            Compute <math id="alg2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm inc}({\bm{a}_{s}^{t,g}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>inc</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm inc}({\bm{a}_{s}^{t,g}})</annotation></semantics></math> for antibody <math id="alg2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{a}_{s}^{t,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{a}_{s}^{t,g}</annotation></semantics></math> according to (<a href="#S5.E53" title="In 5.4 Combinatorial Subproblem ‣ 5 Problem Solution ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">53</span></a>);
</div>
<div id="alg2.4.8" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.4.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">6</span></span>
            Select the top <math id="alg2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{S}{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mi>S</mi><mi>μ</mi></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{S}{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> antibodies with the highest incentive values from <math id="alg2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}^{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>g</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}^{g}</annotation></semantics></math> to constitute <math id="alg2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{\rm imm}^{g+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>imm</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{\rm imm}^{g+1}</annotation></semantics></math> ;
</div>
<div id="alg2.4.9" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.4.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">7</span></span>
            Clone each antibody of <math id="alg2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{\rm imm}^{g+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>imm</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{\rm imm}^{g+1}</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="alg2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> times to obtain the clone set <math id="alg2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{\rm clo}^{g+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>clo</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{\rm clo}^{g+1}</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="alg2.4.10" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.4.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">8</span></span>
            Mutate all antibodies in the clone set <math id="alg2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{\rm clo}^{g+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>clo</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{\rm clo}^{g+1}</annotation></semantics></math> with the mutation rate <math id="alg2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math> of each gene to generate the mutation set <math id="alg2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{\rm mut}^{g+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>mut</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{\rm mut}^{g+1}</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="alg2.4.11" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.4.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">9</span></span>
            Compute the affinity values of all antibodies in <math id="alg2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{\rm mut}^{g+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>mut</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{\rm mut}^{g+1}</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="alg2.4.12" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.4.12.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">10</span></span>
            Select top <math id="alg2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\mu S-S}{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mi>μ</mi></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\mu S-S}{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> antibodies with the highest affinity values from <math id="alg2.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{\rm mut}^{g+1}\bigcup\mathcal{A}_{\rm imm}^{g+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>mut</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⋃</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>imm</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{\rm mut}^{g+1}\bigcup\mathcal{A}_{\rm imm}^{g+1}</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="alg2.4.13" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.4.13.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">11</span></span>
            Obtain the next antibody set <math id="alg2.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}^{g+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}^{g+1}</annotation></semantics></math> with the selected top <math id="alg2.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\mu S-S}{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mi>μ</mi></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\mu S-S}{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> antibodies and the other <math id="alg2.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{S}{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mi>S</mi><mi>μ</mi></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{S}{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> randomly generated antibodies;
</div>
<div id="alg2.4.14" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.4.14.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">12</span></span>
            <span id="alg2.4.14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg2.m27" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{a}^{t*}=\arg\max_{a_{s}^{t,G}\in\mathcal{A}^{G}}{\rm aff}(a_{s}^{t,G})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>arg</mi><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>G</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mi>aff</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{a}^{t*}=\arg\max_{a_{s}^{t,G}\in\mathcal{A}^{G}}{\rm aff}(a_{s}^{t,G})</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="alg2.4.15" class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.4 </span>Combinatorial Subproblem</h3>

<div id="S5.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Although <math id="S5.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textbf{P4.2}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">P4.2</mtext><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textbf{P4.2}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> for attains the optimal bandwidth vector for any given <math id="S5.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{a}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{a}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, a closed-form solution remains intractable, leading to implicit <math id="S5.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{2}(\bm{a}^{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{2}(\bm{a}^{t})</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S5.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textbf{P4.2}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">P4.2</mtext><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textbf{P4.2}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. In such cases, the combinatorial optimization problem <span id="S5.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">P4.1</span> can rely on heuristic algorithms to search for optimal <math id="S5.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{a}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{a}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. In wireless channel allocation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>]</cite> and job scheduling <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">41</a>]</cite>, the immune algorithm has demonstrated superior performance. Furthermore, for <math id="S5.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="J_{1}(\bm{a}^{t},\bm{B}^{t*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝑩</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{1}(\bm{a}^{t},\bm{B}^{t*})</annotation></semantics></math> in <span id="S5.SS4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">P4.1</span>, <math id="S5.SS4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{a}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{a}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is firmly related to which modalities participate in training in the <math id="S5.SS4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>-th communication round. Various participation of modalities causes significant variations in <math id="S5.SS4.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="J_{1}(\bm{a}^{t},\bm{B}^{t*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝑩</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{1}(\bm{a}^{t},\bm{B}^{t*})</annotation></semantics></math>. And the immune algorithm ensures antibody diversity within a generation through antibody concentration <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">42</a>]</cite>, which is suitable for client scheduling involving various participation of modalities.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Set the generation number <math id="S5.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g:=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>:=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g:=0</annotation></semantics></math> and randomly generate the initial antibody set <math id="S5.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}^{0}=\{\bm{a}_{1}^{t,0},\bm{a}_{2}^{t,0},\cdots,\bm{a}_{S}^{t,0}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}^{0}=\{\bm{a}_{1}^{t,0},\bm{a}_{2}^{t,0},\cdots,\bm{a}_{S}^{t,0}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. According to <math id="S5.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{2}(\bm{a}^{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{2}(\bm{a}^{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, the affinity function of antibody <math id="S5.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{a}_{s}^{t,g},s=1,2,\cdots,S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{a}_{s}^{t,g},s=1,2,\cdots,S</annotation></semantics></math> is formulated as</p>
<table id="S5.E50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm aff}(\bm{a}_{s}^{t,g})=(J_{2}^{\max},J_{2}(\bm{a}_{s}^{t,g}))^{\iota}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>aff</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>J</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>max</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>ι</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm aff}(\bm{a}_{s}^{t,g})=(J_{2}^{\max},J_{2}(\bm{a}_{s}^{t,g}))^{\iota},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(50)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S5.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{2}^{\max}\triangleq\max_{s=1,2,\cdots,S}J_{2}(\bm{a}_{s}^{t,g})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>J</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>max</mi></msubsup><mo>≜</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{2}^{\max}\triangleq\max_{s=1,2,\cdots,S}J_{2}(\bm{a}_{s}^{t,g})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\iota" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ι</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\iota</annotation></semantics></math> is a exponential coefficient to adjust dispersion of the affinity function. As for infeasible <math id="S5.SS4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{a}_{s}^{t,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{a}_{s}^{t,g}</annotation></semantics></math>, its affinity function is set to 0.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Computing the similarity from <math id="S5.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{a}_{s}^{t,g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{a}_{s}^{t,g}</annotation></semantics></math> to each antibody in <math id="S5.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}^{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>g</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}^{g}</annotation></semantics></math>, the antibody concentration is</p>
<table id="S5.E51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm con}(\bm{a}_{s}^{t,g})=\frac{1}{S}\sum_{i=1}^{S}{\rm sim}(\bm{a}_{s}^{t,g},\bm{a}_{i}^{t,g})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>con</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>S</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>S</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>sim</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm con}(\bm{a}_{s}^{t,g})=\frac{1}{S}\sum_{i=1}^{S}{\rm sim}(\bm{a}_{s}^{t,g},\bm{a}_{i}^{t,g}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(51)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS4.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where the similarity function <math id="S5.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm sim}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>sim</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm sim}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is determined by comparing the Hamming distance <math id="S5.SS4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm dis}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>dis</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm dis}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> to a threshold <math id="S5.SS4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm Dis}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Dis</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm Dis}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e.,</p>
<table id="S5.E52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm sim}(\bm{a}_{s}^{t,g},\bm{a}_{i}^{t,g})=\begin{cases}1,&{\rm dis}(\bm{a}_{s}^{t,g},\bm{a}_{i}^{t,g})\leq{\rm Dis};\\
0,&{\rm dis}(\bm{a}_{s}^{t,g},\bm{a}_{i}^{t,g})&gt;{\rm Dis}.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>sim</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>dis</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>Dis</mi></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>dis</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>Dis</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm sim}(\bm{a}_{s}^{t,g},\bm{a}_{i}^{t,g})=\begin{cases}1,&amp;{\rm dis}(\bm{a}_{s}^{t,g},\bm{a}_{i}^{t,g})\leq{\rm Dis};\\
0,&amp;{\rm dis}(\bm{a}_{s}^{t,g},\bm{a}_{i}^{t,g})&gt;{\rm Dis}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(52)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The incentive function balancing the affinity function and the diversity function is</p>
<table id="S5.E53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm inc}(\bm{a}_{s}^{t,g})=\epsilon_{1}{\rm aff}(\bm{a}_{s}^{t,g})-\epsilon_{2}{\rm con}(\bm{a}_{s}^{t,g})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>inc</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>aff</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>con</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm inc}(\bm{a}_{s}^{t,g})=\epsilon_{1}{\rm aff}(\bm{a}_{s}^{t,g})-\epsilon_{2}{\rm con}(\bm{a}_{s}^{t,g}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(53)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS4.p4.2" class="ltx_p">According to incentive values of <math id="S5.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}^{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>g</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}^{g}</annotation></semantics></math>, the top <math id="S5.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{S}{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mi>S</mi><mi>μ</mi></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{S}{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> antibodies are selected to constitute <math id="S5.SS4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{\rm imm}^{g+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>imm</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{\rm imm}^{g+1}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S5.SS4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>-fold cloning and mutation. Select the top <math id="S5.SS4.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\mu S-S}{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mi>μ</mi></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\mu S-S}{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> antibodies from <math id="S5.SS4.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{\rm imm}^{g+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>imm</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{\rm imm}^{g+1}</annotation></semantics></math> and mutant antibodies, and generate randomly <math id="S5.SS4.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{S}{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mi>S</mi><mi>μ</mi></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{S}{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> antibodies. The next antibody set <math id="S5.SS4.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}^{g+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}^{g+1}</annotation></semantics></math> is composed by the selected <math id="S5.SS4.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\mu S-S}{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mi>μ</mi></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\mu S-S}{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> antibodies and the generated <math id="S5.SS4.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{S}{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mi>S</mi><mi>μ</mi></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{S}{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> antibodies. Similarly, we can obtain <math id="S5.SS4.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}^{g+2},A^{g+3},\cdots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em">⋯</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}^{g+2},A^{g+3},\cdots</annotation></semantics></math> till the maximal generation number <math id="S5.SS4.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>. And <math id="S5.SS4.p4.m13" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{a}^{t*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">∗</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{a}^{t*}</annotation></semantics></math> is the antibody with the maximal affinity in <math id="S5.SS4.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}^{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>G</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}^{G}</annotation></semantics></math>. The detailed process is presented in <span id="S5.SS4.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="In 5.3 Continuous Subproblem ‣ 5 Problem Solution ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></span>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.5 </span>Computational Complexity Analysis</h3>

<div id="S5.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The complexity of solving the continuous subproblem comes from the Newton iteration in (<a href="#S5.E41" title="In 5.3 Continuous Subproblem ‣ 5 Problem Solution ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">41</span></a>), (<a href="#S5.E44" title="In 5.3 Continuous Subproblem ‣ 5 Problem Solution ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">44</span></a>), and (<a href="#S5.E46" title="In 5.3 Continuous Subproblem ‣ 5 Problem Solution ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">46</span></a>) or (<a href="#S5.E48" title="In 5.3 Continuous Subproblem ‣ 5 Problem Solution ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">48</span></a>). Given convergence thresholds <math id="S5.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\tau},\epsilon_{B},\epsilon_{\kappa}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\tau},\epsilon_{B},\epsilon_{\kappa}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S5.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau^{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>τ</mi><mi>max</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau^{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B^{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>B</mi><mi>max</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B^{\max}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>, the computational complexity of the worst case is <math id="S5.SS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}\big(U^{2}\log(\frac{1}{\epsilon_{\kappa}})+U\log(\frac{1}{\epsilon_{B}})\log(\frac{1}{\epsilon_{\kappa}})+U\log(\frac{1}{\epsilon_{\tau}})\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}\big(U^{2}\log(\frac{1}{\epsilon_{\kappa}})+U\log(\frac{1}{\epsilon_{B}})\log(\frac{1}{\epsilon_{\kappa}})+U\log(\frac{1}{\epsilon_{\tau}})\big)</annotation></semantics></math>.
As for the combinatorial subproblem, the complexity is positively related to <math id="S5.SS5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus the computational complexity of <span id="S5.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="In 5.3 Continuous Subproblem ‣ 5 Problem Solution ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></span> is <math id="S5.SS5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(SG)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(SG)</annotation></semantics></math>.
The total complexity of the solution is <math id="S5.SS5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}\big(SGU^{2}\log(\frac{1}{\epsilon_{\kappa}})+SGU\log(\frac{1}{\epsilon_{B}})\log(\frac{1}{\epsilon_{\kappa}})+SGU\log(\frac{1}{\epsilon_{\tau}})\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>κ</mi></msub></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}\big(SGU^{2}\log(\frac{1}{\epsilon_{\kappa}})+SGU\log(\frac{1}{\epsilon_{B}})\log(\frac{1}{\epsilon_{\kappa}})+SGU\log(\frac{1}{\epsilon_{\tau}})\big)</annotation></semantics></math>. However, benefiting from the parallel computing among antibodies and clients, the actual computational time can be reduced to <math id="S5.SS5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{SU}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{SU}</annotation></semantics></math> of the computational complexity.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">6 </span>Numerical Results</h2>

<div id="S6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the experiment, a base station (BS) connected to a server and <math id="S6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> clients are set in a circular network area to collaboratively complete wireless MFL tasks. All clients are uniformly distributed within a 500-meter radius. Other parameters of wireless MFL are listed in Table <a href="#S6.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 6 Numerical Results ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S6.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span>System Parameters</figcaption>
<table id="S6.T2.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S6.T2.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S6.T2.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt"><span id="S6.T2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Parameter</span></td>
