<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S6.F6.sf4.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(d)</span> </span><span id="S6.F6.sf4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Text Accuracy</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span>Multimodal accuracy, unimodal accuracy and energy consumption curves in all communication rounds on IEMOCAP.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.3 </span>MFL on IEMOCAP</h3>

<div id="S6.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fig. <a href="#S6.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ 6.2 MFL on CREMA-D ‣ 6 Numerical Results ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> shows multimodal performance, unimodal performance, and energy consumption of five algorithms on IEMOCAP. From Fig. <a href="#S6.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ 6.2 MFL on CREMA-D ‣ 6 Numerical Results ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> (a)-(d), we observe the following trends: The JCSBA algorithm consistently outperforms other algorithms in the multimodal performance, unimodal performance, and energy consumption. The Dropout algorithm converges faster than the Selection algorithm in the unimodal accuracy on the text modality. However, despite lagging behind, the Selection algorithm eventually surpasses the Dropout algorithm in the multimodal accuracy. Moreover, the Random algorithm and Round-Robin algorithms exhibit the worst performance and highest energy consumption. The above results align with the results in Section VI-B and have similar reasons, validating the general applicability of the JCSBA algorithm. The detailed multimodal and unimodal accuracies of all algorithms are summarized in Table <a href="#S6.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 6.2 MFL on CREMA-D ‣ 6 Numerical Results ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Comparing Fig. <a href="#S6.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ 6.2 MFL on CREMA-D ‣ 6 Numerical Results ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> (c) and (d), we can see that the audio modality converges faster than the text modality on IEMOCAP. This further demonstrates that different convergence rates among modalities are common in multimodal learning. Hence, it is vital for an MFL algorithm to schedule clients with modality heterogeneity in consideration of the convergence process of all modalities.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S7" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">7 </span>Conclusions</h2>

<div id="S7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this paper, we have proposed the JCSBA algorithm for wireless MFL on modal heterogeneity to enhance both the multimodal performance and the unimodal performance. The wireless MFL architecture has employed the decision-level fusion and added the unimodal loss in local updates and the objective function. Building on the architecture, the JCSBA algorithm has adaptively scheduled clients for convergence of all modalities and allocated bandwidth to ensure clients with modal heterogeneity participating in MFL within latency. The experiments on multimodal datasets have validated the performance gain of our JCSBA algorithm.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.p2.1" class="ltx_p">As for potential future works, modality heterogeneity in MFL could be extended to the sample level, where different samples of a client correspond to heterogeneous modalities <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">25</a>]</cite>. Additionally, clients can flexibly select a subset of their available modalities for training according to wireless constraints and MFL performance. In such cases, modeling the latency and the energy consumption would become quite difficult, making performance analysis and optimization even more challenging but also more meaningful.</p>
</div>
<section id="A0.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">.1 </span>Proof of Theorem 1 </h3>

<div id="A0.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A0.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">With <span id="A0.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption2" title="Assumption 2. ‣ 4.1 Definition and Assumption ‣ 4 MFL Performance Analysis ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></span>, the difference of loss functions are transformed into the difference of models as</p>
<table id="A0.E54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A0.E54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(\bm{\theta}^{t})-H(\bm{\psi}^{t})\leq|H(\bm{\theta}^{t})-H(\bm{\psi}^{t})|\leq\rho\|\bm{\theta}^{t}-\bm{\psi}^{t}\|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝝍</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝝍</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝝍</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\bm{\theta}^{t})-H(\bm{\psi}^{t})\leq|H(\bm{\theta}^{t})-H(\bm{\psi}^{t})|\leq\rho\|\bm{\theta}^{t}-\bm{\psi}^{t}\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(54)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A0.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Each model can be divided into <math id="A0.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> submodels, which helps to express the norm as</p>
<table id="A0.E55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A0.E55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\|\bm{\theta}^{t}-\bm{\psi}^{t}\|=\rho\sqrt{\sum_{m=1}^{M}\|\bm{\theta}^{t}_{m}-\bm{\psi}^{t}_{m}\|^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝝍</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>𝝍</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\|\bm{\theta}^{t}-\bm{\psi}^{t}\|=\rho\sqrt{\sum_{m=1}^{M}\|\bm{\theta}^{t}_{m}-\bm{\psi}^{t}_{m}\|^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(55)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A0.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A0.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For modality <math id="A0.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>, there is either <math id="A0.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\in\mathcal{M}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\in\mathcal{M}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A0.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\notin\mathcal{M}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∉</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\notin\mathcal{M}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. With <math id="A0.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\theta}^{t}_{{\rm g},m}=\bm{\theta}^{t-1}_{{\rm g},m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\theta}^{t}_{{\rm g},m}=\bm{\theta}^{t-1}_{{\rm g},m}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A0.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\notin\mathcal{M}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∉</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\notin\mathcal{M}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <span id="A0.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition <a href="#Thmdefinition1" title="Definition 1. ‣ 4.1 Definition and Assumption ‣ 4 MFL Performance Analysis ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></span>, the difference of the two unimodal submodels for <math id="A0.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\notin\mathcal{M}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∉</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\notin\mathcal{M}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="A0.E56" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A0.E56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t}-\bm{\psi}_{m}^{t}\|^{2}=\eta^{2}\|\nabla H(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})\|^{2}\leq\eta^{2}(\zeta_{m}^{t-1})^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>𝝍</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>ζ</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t}-\bm{\psi}_{m}^{t}\|^{2}=\eta^{2}\|\nabla H(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})\|^{2}\leq\eta^{2}(\zeta_{m}^{t-1})^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(56)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A0.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">As for <math id="A0.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\in\mathcal{M}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\in\mathcal{M}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, (<a href="#S2.E12" title="In 2.2 Partial Participation of Wireless Clients ‣ 2 Multimodal Federated Learning Framework over Wireless Networks ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>) and <span id="A0.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition <a href="#Thmdefinition1" title="Definition 1. ‣ 4.1 Definition and Assumption ‣ 4 MFL Performance Analysis ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></span> are used to expand the difference as</p>
<table id="A0.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A0.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A0.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t}-\bm{\psi}^{t}_{m}\|^{2}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>𝝍</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t}-\bm{\psi}^{t}_{m}\|^{2}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A0.Ex18.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\eta^{2}\Big\|\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}_{m}^{t}}(w_{k,m}^{t}-\bar{w}_{k,m})\nabla H_{k}(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.600em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eta^{2}\Big\|\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}_{m}^{t}}(w_{k,m}^{t}-\bar{w}_{k,m})\nabla H_{k}(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A0.E57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A0.E57.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-\!\!\!\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}_{m}\backslash\mathcal{K}_{m}^{t}}\!\!\!\bar{w}_{k,m}\nabla H_{k}(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})\Big\|^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.462em;" width="0.462em"><mo>−</mo></mpadded><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.600em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.0835em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\!\!\!\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}_{m}\backslash\mathcal{K}_{m}^{t}}\!\!\!\bar{w}_{k,m}\nabla H_{k}(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})\Big\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(57)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A0.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Adding two zero terms <math id="A0.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\big[\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}_{m}^{t}}(w_{k,m}^{t}-\bar{w}_{k,m})\nabla H(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big[\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}_{m}^{t}}(w_{k,m}^{t}-\bar{w}_{k,m})\nabla H(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})</annotation></semantics></math>
<math id="A0.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="-\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}_{m}^{t}}(w_{k,m}^{t}-\bar{w}_{k,m})\nabla H(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}_{m}^{t}}(w_{k,m}^{t}-\bar{w}_{k,m})\nabla H(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})\big]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A0.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\big[\nabla H(\bm{\theta}^{t-1}_{{\rm g},m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big[\nabla H(\bm{\theta}^{t-1}_{{\rm g},m})</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A0.SS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="-\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}_{m}^{t}}\bar{w}_{k,m}\nabla H(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}_{m}^{t}}\bar{w}_{k,m}\nabla H(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})\big]</annotation></semantics></math> into (<a href="#A0.E57" title="In .1 Proof of Theorem 1 ‣ 7 Conclusions ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">57</span></a>), we then rearrange and combine terms to obtain an equation as</p>
<table id="A0.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A0.E58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A0.E58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t}-\bm{\psi}^{t}_{m}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>𝝍</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t}-\bm{\psi}^{t}_{m}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(58)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A0.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A0.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\eta^{2}\Big\|\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}_{m}^{t}}(w_{k,m}^{t}-\bar{w}_{k,m})\nabla H_{k}(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.600em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\eta^{2}\Big\|\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}_{m}^{t}}(w_{k,m}^{t}-\bar{w}_{k,m})\nabla H_{k}(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A0.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A0.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\quad-\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}_{m}^{t}}(w_{k,m}^{t}-\bar{w}_{k,m})\nabla H(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\quad-\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}_{m}^{t}}(w_{k,m}^{t}-\bar{w}_{k,m})\nabla H(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A0.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A0.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\quad+\!\!\!\!\!\!\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}_{m}\backslash\mathcal{K}_{m}^{t}}\!\!\!\!\!\!\bar{w}_{k,m}\nabla H(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})-\!\!\!\!\!\!\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}_{m}\backslash\mathcal{K}_{m}^{t}}\!\!\!\!\!\!\bar{w}_{k,m}\nabla H_{k}(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})\Big\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0em;" width="0em"><mo>+</mo></mpadded><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mpadded style="width:0em;" width="0em"><mo>−</mo></mpadded><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.600em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\quad+\!\!\!\!\!\!\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}_{m}\backslash\mathcal{K}_{m}^{t}}\!\!\!\!\!\!\bar{w}_{k,m}\nabla H(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})-\!\!\!\!\!\!\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}_{m}\backslash\mathcal{K}_{m}^{t}}\!\!\!\!\!\!\bar{w}_{k,m}\nabla H_{k}(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})\Big\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A0.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A0.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\eta^{2}\Big\|\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}_{m}^{t}}\!(w_{k,m}^{t}-\bar{w}_{k,m})(\nabla H_{k}(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})-\nabla H(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\eta^{2}\Big\|\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}_{m}^{t}}\!(w_{k,m}^{t}-\bar{w}_{k,m})(\nabla H_{k}(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})-\nabla H(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A0.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A0.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\quad-\!\!\!\!\!\!\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}_{m}\backslash\mathcal{K}_{m}^{t}}\!\!\!\!\!\!\bar{w}_{k,m}(\nabla H_{k}(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})\!-\!\nabla H(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1}))\Big\|^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0em;" width="0em"><mo>−</mo></mpadded><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">−</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.600em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.0835em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\quad-\!\!\!\!\!\!\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}_{m}\backslash\mathcal{K}_{m}^{t}}\!\!\!\!\!\!\bar{w}_{k,m}(\nabla H_{k}(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})\!-\!\nabla H(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1}))\Big\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A0.SS1.p2.4" class="ltx_p">Dividing the square norm in (<a href="#A0.E58" title="In .1 Proof of Theorem 1 ‣ 7 Conclusions ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">58</span></a>) into two terms according to <math id="A0.SS1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\bm{\varphi}_{1}-\bm{\varphi}_{2}\|^{2}\leq\|\bm{\varphi}_{1}\|^{2}+2\|\bm{\varphi}_{2}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝝋</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝝋</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝝋</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝝋</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\bm{\varphi}_{1}-\bm{\varphi}_{2}\|^{2}\leq\|\bm{\varphi}_{1}\|^{2}+2\|\bm{\varphi}_{2}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we then obtain</p>
<table id="A0.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A0.E59"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A0.E59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\bm{\theta}^{t}_{{\rm{g},m}}-\bm{\psi}^{t}_{m}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>𝝍</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\bm{\theta}^{t}_{{\rm{g},m}}-\bm{\psi}^{t}_{m}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(59)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A0.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A0.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2\eta^{2}\Big\|\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}_{m}^{t}}(w_{k,m}^{t}-\bar{w}_{k,m})(\nabla H_{k}(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})-\nabla H(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})\Big\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.600em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.600em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2\eta^{2}\Big\|\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}_{m}^{t}}(w_{k,m}^{t}-\bar{w}_{k,m})(\nabla H_{k}(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})-\nabla H(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})\Big\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A0.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A0.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+2\eta^{2}\Big\|\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}_{m}\backslash\mathcal{K}_{m}^{t}}\bar{w}_{k,m}(\nabla H_{k}(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})-\nabla H(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})\Big\|^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.600em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.600em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.0835em">.</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+2\eta^{2}\Big\|\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}_{m}\backslash\mathcal{K}_{m}^{t}}\bar{w}_{k,m}(\nabla H_{k}(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})-\nabla H(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})\Big\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A0.SS1.p2.5" class="ltx_p">The weighted sum of gradient differences in (<a href="#A0.E59" title="In .1 Proof of Theorem 1 ‣ 7 Conclusions ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">59</span></a>) is hard to tackle. To construct <math id="A0.SS1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\nabla H_{k}(\bm{\theta}_{m}^{t-1})-\nabla H(\bm{\theta}^{t-1})\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\nabla H_{k}(\bm{\theta}_{m}^{t-1})-\nabla H(\bm{\theta}^{t-1})\|</annotation></semantics></math> with Jensen’s inequality, we first normalize the weights as</p>
<table id="A0.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A0.E60"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A0.E60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\bm{\theta}^{t}_{{\rm g},m}-\bm{\psi}^{t}_{m}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>𝝍</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\bm{\theta}^{t}_{{\rm g},m}-\bm{\psi}^{t}_{m}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(60)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A0.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A0.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\Big\|\!\!\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}_{m}^{t}}\!\!\!\frac{w_{k,m}^{t}-\bar{w}_{k,m}}{1-\sum_{i\in\mathcal{K}_{m}^{t}}\!\bar{w}_{i,m}}(\nabla H_{k}(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})-\nabla H(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1}))\Big\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.410em;" width="0.410em"><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mpadded><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\Big\|\!\!\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}_{m}^{t}}\!\!\!\frac{w_{k,m}^{t}-\bar{w}_{k,m}}{1-\sum_{i\in\mathcal{K}_{m}^{t}}\!\bar{w}_{i,m}}(\nabla H_{k}(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})-\nabla H(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1}))\Big\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A0.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A0.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\times 2\eta^{2}(1-\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}_{m}^{t}}\bar{w}_{k,m})^{2}+2\eta^{2}(1-\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}_{m}^{t}}\bar{w}_{k,m})^{2}\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\times 2\eta^{2}(1-\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}_{m}^{t}}\bar{w}_{k,m})^{2}+2\eta^{2}(1-\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}_{m}^{t}}\bar{w}_{k,m})^{2}\times</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A0.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A0.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\Big\|\!\!\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}_{m}\backslash\mathcal{K}_{m}^{t}}\!\!\!\!\frac{\bar{w}_{k,m}}{1-\sum_{i\in\mathcal{K}_{m}^{t}}\bar{w}_{i,m}}(\nabla H_{k}(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})-\nabla H(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1}))\Big\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.410em;" width="0.410em"><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mpadded><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜽</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\Big\|\!\!\sum_{k\in\mathcal{K}_{m}\backslash\mathcal{K}_{m}^{t}}\!\!\!\!\frac{\bar{w}_{k,m}}{1-\sum_{i\in\mathcal{K}_{m}^{t}}\bar{w}_{i,m}}(\nabla H_{k}(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1})-\nabla H(\bm{\theta}_{{\rm g},m}^{t-1}))\Big\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A0.SS1.p2.6" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A0.SS1.p2.m14" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is convex, Jensen’ inequality can be applied in (<a href="#A0.E60" title="In .1 Proof of Theorem 1 ‣ 7 Conclusions ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">60</span></a>). And <span id="A0.SS1.p2.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption <a href="#Thmassumption4" title="Assumption 4. ‣ 4.1 Definition and Assumption ‣ 4 MFL Performance Analysis ‣ Analysis and Optimization of Wireless Multimodal Federated Learning on Modal Heterogeneity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a></span> is then used to enlarge the gradient difference into</p>
<table id="A0.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A0.E61"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
